-- Which failing record field is reported must not depend on symbol
-- id order: `f g` fails on both `alpha` and `omega`, and the one named is
-- the first by name TEXT, `alpha`, whose inner record lacks `apple`
-- (checker-v2.md §7.2). Naming `beta`, `omega`'s
-- inner field, because `omega` is written first in `f`'s annotation and so
-- interned first — while the same file with the annotation's two fields
-- swapped names `apple` — would let interning choose. Field order in a
-- record type means nothing, so the choice must follow the program's text.
--
-- One file on purpose: across modules the ids also depend on which worker
-- lexed which file, so a two-module form (`Aaa` + `Main`) would be
-- red only most of the time at `--jobs` > 1.

f : { omega : { beta : Int }, alpha : { apple : Int } } -> Int
f r = 0


g : { alpha : { cherry : Int }, omega : { delta : Int } }
g = { alpha = { cherry = 1 }, omega = { delta = 2 } }


main = f g
